X-Complaints-To: newsabuse@supernews.com

Just update to the latest firmware, SRM will be there. In alphabios

goto setup (F2)
cmos settings
Advanced  (F6)
3/4 down the screen is the console selection, select "SRM UNIX"
save settings
cycle power


to switch back at the SRM console prompt ">>>" type      "set os_type nt"
followed by a carriage return then power cycle.

The 433-600 a +au run with either milo or aboot, your better off with SRM.

When installing redhat using SRM you MUST use "CUSTOM INSTALL"
Then use fdisk to partition the disk with BSD style disk labels  NOT FAT
Style.
after the install, reboot using the floppy but setting root to your hard
disk partition containing the root.
then use swriteboot to write bootlx to the boot blocks on the hard drive.

use the DS20 SRM instructions on

 http://www.digital.com/alphaserver/linux/install_guide.html

As a guide, an SRM install is an SRM install regardless of Alpha Platform if
you use the Generic kernel and the latest ramdisk from errata.redhat.com

http://www.redhat.com/corp/support/errata/boot99_05_29.html

JJ

