be able to get a 2.5" SCSI drive of usable capacity so you can go
external SCSI or get a normal 2.5" IDE laptop drive with a 44 pin
interface (the power comes through the ribbon). The cable is the
tricky bit here. In the UK you can get one from HCP on 07000 784648.
It should be possible to cram a 3.5" disk inside if you don't want to
use the PCI slot (assuming you have a PCI slot) but you will have to
knock up some brackets yourself. There may be some issues with the
power connector as well.
I found an internal IDE to be half as fast as an external SCSI which
makes a significant difference on a machine that is none too speedy to
begin with.

Martin



