I just decided to get my modem out of my intel linux box, and put it
in my alpha (axppci33). In my intel machine it worked right away on
com1,
but in the alpha I jumpered it to com4 (otherwise I didn't get response
from it) and changed the symbolic link /dev/modem accordingly.
Then I added an ppp0 device to my machine (I checked and double checked
everything on my Intel) and did a: ifup ppp0
The modem started to make some noise, but nothing happened, after a
tail /var/log/messages, I saw this message: Serial Line looped back.
Well nothing the PPP-HOWTO couldn't fix, just add the line
lcp-max-configure 30
to my /etc/ppp/options and it should work, well it didn't so I tried 
300 and 3000 instead of 30, but stil my serial line got looped back.
Well, lets try the -mn option in /etc/ppp/options (with this option 
pppd shouldn't detected a looped back serial line), for a moment 
everything looked okay. For a moment! 
The Local and Remote IP adresses i got "assigned" are both 192.168.3.1 
(which is the address of my eth0). The routes are okay (same as on the
Intel machine), just did a: route add default ppp0, to make sure.

I am out of options, please help.

