At the moment jensens seem to flood the market, so actually quite a lot
of people try to install rh6.0. In my humble opinion the real problem
still is to get a working and recent initial kernel to put in the aboot
boot area (copyboot and, once the system is up, swriteboot do that for
you). It might be of interest to you to subscribe to the redhat axp
mailing list as most of the recent jensen discussion is going on there.
(I am sure we will be able to get all the machines up and running after
some struggle)

Good luck...
