To me it sounds like you tried to mount the 'uninitialized' harddisk as 
root filesystem instead of root filesystem image on floppy or CD. Should 
not matter what is on the harddisk when one starts installing the system. 
If you just low-level format it, then it certainly will not have any 
better partition table at all.

I suggest you read the instructions again and use 'load_ramdisk=1' and 
'root=/dev/fd0' as boot parameters in case of loading root image from a 
floppy disk.

