Konrad Hinsen wrote:
> 
> I am trying to install some numerical code on an Alpha system running
> RedHat 6.0, and I get lots of crashes. It seems that the math library
> generates a floating point exception in many cases (e.g. log(-1.))
> where I'd rather like to get an error code back to my routines.
> Is there any way to change this?
> --

Sure ... install a signal  handler:

in the main prog call 


   (void) signal(SIGFPE, error_handler);

where you can define the error handler yourself e.g.



error_handler(err_sig)
int             err_sig;
{
 /** do something here **/
}

You have to include signal.h of course .. 

