References: <37D63DB5.E203CCF5@nat.vu.nl> <37D68EE8.7DAD324D@percy.engr.wisc.edu>
Organization: Scifi Communications International Oy, http://www.sci.fi/, helpdesk@sci.fi, (3)2899111
Newsgroups: comp.os.linux.alpha

This is how I installed the beta version of 'ccc' on my Debian GNU/Linux 
2.1 system. (Compaq C T6.2-001 on Linux 2.2.12 alpha)

First, gcc needs to be installed with normal libraries and all the 
important stuff. My system has gcc version egcs-2.91.60 Debian 2.1 
(egcs-1.1.1 release).

--- clip ---

converted RPM to DEB package with 'alien':

  alien libots-2.2.6-1.alpha.rpm
  alien ccc-6.2.0-2.alpha.rpm

installed the packages with 'dpkg':

  dpkg --install libots_2.2.6-2_alpha.deb
  dpkg --install ccc_6.2.0-3_alpha.deb

changed the current directory:

  cd /usr/lib/compaq/ccc-6.2/alpha-redhat-linux/bin/

edited three paths in 'create-comp-config.sh':

  from: /usr/lib/gcc-lib/alpha-redhat-linux
  to:   /usr/lib/gcc-lib/alpha-linux

  from: /usr/alpha-redhat-linux/include
  to:   /usr/include

  from: /usr/alpha-redhat-linux/lib
  to:   /usr/lib

executed 'create-comp-config.sh'

  ./create-comp-config.sh

--- clip ---

After all this I managed to compile ssh-1.2.27 successfully with 'ccc' as 
the compiler, so I assume it is installed correctly.

