> 
> 
> Is this expected performance or can I do better? I know there is a beta
> c compiler from compaq but I really need c++ for most of my work.

In a different thread (~1 week ago), i wrote something about ieee and
arithmetic exceptions. I've now experimented some more and found the
following:
  o the performance hit one gets from using the -mieee flag with gcc
    depends largely on the sort of fp one is doing: with tons of
    simple arithmetic like multiplications and subtractions, the hit
    can be considerable while with more complex things like sine and
    exponentials, it's not much.
  o compaq's libcpml is _fast_ and does the right thing wrt to
    arithmetic exceptions. I've put that lib in place, compiled with
    gcc -mieee -lcpml and now my SX164 533 blows away all pentia[1].  (My 
    code mainly consumes time in a rather small loop with lots of
    cos() exp() and the like)
  o given the fact above, I've changed my mind wrt to exception
    handling; I'm now using the -mieee flag and gcc since I have yet
    to get ccc to compile my main application (Khoros image
    manipulation from www.khoral.com if that matters).


[1] well, at least all that I have access to. Fastest of them is a
    dual P3-450 where the main loop of my code is not parallelized;
    the SX is still about 1.5 times faster.

The problem that I still have is that ccc gives me unresolved symbols
in some places. (__builtin_next_arg and the like; I guess, I still
don't have all the libs in place or am missing some includes... )

