Well it works for me :)
Really.

1. The IRQ dosen't wotk in linux. Forget you ever saw that.
Here are my ,config sections from the kernel

CONFIG_PARPORT=m
CONFIG_PARPORT_PC=m
# CONFIG_PARPORT_OTHER is not set

#
# Plug and Play support
#
CONFIG_PNP=y
# CONFIG_PNP_PARPORT is not set


CONFIG_PRINTER=m
CONFIG_PRINTER_READBACK=y


This is from/etc/conf.modules

alias   parport_lowlevel parport_pc
options parport_pc io=0x3bc irq=auto
options lp  parport=0



