"Bruce Rannala (Admin Account)" �ۼ�:

> Anyone out there installed redhat 6.0 on a Compaq/DEC "professional
> workstation"  XP1000 machine? I am having trouble getting the partitions
> formatted on my harddrive when using BSD disk labels. The HD is a DEC
> model RZ2CD-KS (4.2 GB) on scsi id 0. The system hangs when I attempt to
> install an ext2 filesystem on /dev/sda2. I used fdisk to create my
> partition table as follows:
>     size           offset    fstype
> a: 144585    32130    swap    # (Cyl. 15*- 79*)
> b: 8193150    192780    ext2    # (Cyl. 86*- 3711*)
> c: 8385930    0    unused    0    0    # (Cyl. 1- 3711*)
> fdisk recommends starting the first partition at cylinder 2. I assume
> that this does not apply to the whole disk partition c?
> Any suggestions would be greatly appreciated.
> Bruce

If you go to bsd partition tool, you can see the whole bsd partition 'c'.
At first, delete this partition 'c' - whole disk partition after that create
new partition.
In my experience, if swap partition is located at first, booting fails.

1. Delete patition 'c'
2. create new partition from cylinder 3
3. If possible don't place swap in the fisrt partition.

--
