Yes, good point.

The 21272 core logic chipset provides two 256-bit memory buses (288-bit
incl. ECC) with two arrays of 4 SODIMM. The 21264 is supported by the
21272, with a *256-bit memory interface*. The external L2 cache
subsystem on the daughtercard uses a 128-bit data bus.

This is technically different than a *512-bit* memory path. Still, it
does account for a higher bandwidth.

The bottom line here is that the DS20 has wider bandwidth than the
UP2000 and if you fill all 4 arrays, the performance is enhanced
further.



