Se�n � Donnchadha <sean@forget.about.it> wrote:

> Also, how does the package manager know whether it's safe to update a
> library in use by multiple applications?

It's Just Safe.  If you're replacing an existing file, you just unlink
the old one and write a new one.  Programs using the old one continue to
do so because the inode hangs around until its usage count hits zero.
New programs use the new version.

If you're not replacing an existing file, you've got no worries anyway.

