All,
    I'm trying to re-compile the kernel b/c I'm getting some weird
networking errors on this box (probably b/c I managed to compile and
load the modules but not the new kernel).  Here's the procedure
I followed:
1) make clean
2) make menuconfig
3) make dep
4) make boot
5) make modules
6) make modules_install

I then copied the new kernel located in
/usr/src/linux/arch/alpha/boot/vmlinuz.gz into /boot which is mounted on
/dev/hda7.  The root directory is mounted on /dev/hda5.  I renamed this
file vmlinuz-2.2.5-16-1 and created a soft lnk called vmlinuz1.  I then
re-booted the machine.  At the milo prompt I entered:
boot hda7:vmlinuz1 root=/dev/hda5 load_ramdisk

milo gets to the first line of the boot where it displays the kennel
version and create time and then locks hard.  Changing the milo boot
line back to vmlinuz instead (pointing to the old kernel) and the
machine boots fine.

I know on the PC boxes you have to run lilo again to install the new
kernel; is there an applicable action on the alpha?  From what I've
learned of the boot process so far, it seems to me that the above should
work.

I'm hoping this will solve me networking problems; I'm getting unaligned
trap errors on ping, even to the loopback.  That can't be good...

Thanks in advance for any help...




