> of shared libraries (aside from disk/memory usage) is independent
> field-ugradability, which results in the runtime coupling of two
> binary components that may not have been lab-tested in combination. In
> this particular case, there's no way to eliminate the risk without
> also eliminating the benefit.

        You *can* get around this, as long as it is possible for the
application to request a particular version (major version, minor
version, directory...)

