  AFIAK, Linux doesn't run on the DEC 3000 series.  The current
Alpha/Linux code base assumes that an Alpha handles interrupt similar to
a PC.  Most of the supported Alphas are PCI/ISA and a few EISA. (Correct
me if I'm wrong.)  The 3000s are TurboChannel, and have some funny
interrupt handling.  IIRC, one of the *BSDs will run on it, I don't
remember which one, and even supports the local console now.

