sean@forget.about.it (Se�n � Donnchadha) writes:

> Please. Unix's notion of "versioned shared libraries" is a version
> number placed into the filename. Well, Windows can do that too, and
> often does (MFC.DLL -> MFC20.DLL -> MFC40.DLL -> MFC42.DLL, etc.). But
