wetboy wrote:
> 
> In comp.lang.c Paul Lutus <nospam@nosite.com> wrote:
> :> Now I know you are a better C programmer than I.
> 
> : "Than me" in this case.
> 
> No.  "Than I" is correct.

I rarely find myself agreeing with "wetboy", but since Paul seems to
enjoy correcting grammar and spelling errors, I thought I would join in.
The reason that wetboy is correct is that the above sentence contains an
ellipsis.  In full form, it is
   "Now I know you are a better C programmer than I [am]."

Since 'are' is a copulative verb requiring a nominative predicate, it is
difficult to produce a sentence in which Paul could be right on any
meaning for the sentence.



