>Craig Kelley <ink@inconnu.isu.edu> wrote:
>
>>2)  Many installations simply ignore embedded versioning and simply 
>>    copy the files over.
>>
>
>A broken installation program isn't exactly Windows' fault. What does
>Linux do to prevent programs from blowing away system components?

Linux provides standard tools (e.g. rpm) for installing system components.
These tools, which are part of the OS, do the installation of system
components.  The individual programs themselves do not install the system
components, they just list which system components they need, and let
the package manager deal with it.

