Ted <goodseed@hotmail.com> writes:

>Hi.
>Does anyone know where to get a power supply for DEC PC164 motherboard for 
>Alpha? It has a ATX form factor, however, it does not work with regular ATX 
>power supply.

It "almost" does. It seems that the boards were originally sold with
"Emacs" branded power supplies (yes, really), which had a physical on/off
switch and ignored the soft-power-on from the motherboard. Good thing, too,
as the PC164 motherboard doesn't actually provide any way for the user to
connect a switch to soft-power-on.

If you have a PC164 with a bog standard ATX power supply, then you can
make it go with a soldering iron. Simply attach a small piece of wire
between the 3rd and 4th contact from the right in the top row (when
looking from the power connector edge of the board towards the CPU)
--- it's quite easy to do, and will set the soft-power-on function
