What the hey? You didn't initialize the variable! It has nothing useful
in it. Maybe a compiler set for maximal debugging will automatically
initialize your automatics to 0, but you're certainly not guaranteed it
in general. Most compilers will give you an error message at this code,
because you used a variable before it was set.

Why wouldn't a compiler always set all the automatics to 0? Because it
takes time! Time that could murder a speed-critical function. So they
let you initialize your own darn variables to whatever you want.

Hope this helps,
Bill

