Other OSes have the luxury of savvy users. A Linux app can include a
README saying "This program requires libfoo-1.2.3" and leave it up to
the user to figure out how to set that up without killing another
program that requires libfoo-1.2.2. Windows apps have no such option;
they *MUST* install the libraries they need without the user's help.

>
>They
>also tend to use something as simple as file names that contain the
>version number, so that if an interface incompatible version is installed
>(consciously by the system administrator during an upgrade or patch),
