>
>Really, it shouldn't take much to solve the DLL mess.  Just enforce
>the idea that only service packs or patches distributed by the OS
>vendor should be updating the system directories; applications should
>keep out of the system directories when installing themselves.
>

This wouldn't solve the problem, and it's kind of impractical anway.

>
>And make incompatible versions have different names.
>

I'm afraid you don't understand the problem (no offense intended). All
library updates, no matter how minor, are incompatible. The classic
example is the app whose author accidentally made it depend on buggy
behavior in a library. The library author issues what he believes to
be a harmless and compatible bug fix, but ends up breaking the app
anyway.



