I have to agree with Chad, here; it strains credulity that Microsoft
would wilfully and maliciously sabotage its own software
in an attempt to antagonize users, even if under the guise of "upgrading
for the future".

But anything can happen by accident, or by poor planning.
My guess is that Microsoft may not have sufficiently
researched the issue of reading in Word 2 documents into its latest
and greatest stuff, and, because the saving format is partially
dependent on OLE -- which means, other components -- things
could get mucked up real easily if said subcomponents
don't follow the rules (if one can determine what precisely
the rules are; this feels a bit like the Amiga IFF issue, in a weird
sort of way -- however, one important difference is that the Amiga
IFF file was well-documented, whereas the OLE format is either
not documented, or only documented internally).

So which is it?

[1] Microsoft is evil.
[2] Microsoft is incompetent.
[3] Third-party vendors are evil.
[4] Third-party vendors are incompetent.
[5] It's gotta be the hardware.

