There is no good JIT available for Alpha/Linux.  Digital had ported the
JDK with a working JIT for Alpha/NT and DU.  Neither is useable on Linux.

The Cacao project is a clean-room Java implementation with a fast JIT for
Alpha.  Unfortunately, last I checked it was still a subset of Java 1.0.

Kaffe had lingering support for Alpha, but the releases I tried were
spotty.

The best bet today is by far the native compilers.   Gcj from Cygnus
works on Alpha/Linux today and is very fast, but has no AWT yet.  Toba has
ceased development but is more complete; it uses classes.zip from JDK 1.1.
I have patched Toba to build on Alpha/Linux with good results.

Jeff

