Randall Parker wrote:
> 
> In article <gk95r7.gm2.ln@snowwhite>,
> rsimpson@ewrcsdra.CutThisOut.demon.co.uk says...
> > Are you sure that that is correct?  I understood that the 21264 stopped at
> > 500 MHz and that the 667 MHz chips were the 21264a (EV67) chips?
> 
> Clock speed aside, what is the difference between 21264 and 21264a?
> 
> Is the first one EV6 and the second EV67?

AFAIK, the first one was EV57, which means that process technology
(5=0.35u) is as usual way behind design (7 = 7th design step or so)
The EV67 is the same processor in a better process (6=0.25u), but it
still behind (state of the art is about 0.18u and copper). This is the
main reason why the EV67 is faster than EV57

And yes, UP2000/EV67 combinations are offerd by a number of vendors,
even here in Switzerland :-)

Regards
Alex



