first sorry for not posting the answer, but i assumed it was easy
to spot after a closer look. second sorry for not posting earlier,
but i was out of town all day.


you need to tell the compiler where the libs and includes are, i.e
you have to add the following lines at compile-time:

-I/usr/lib/gcc-lib/alpha-redhat-linux/egcs-2.91.66/include
-L/usr/lib/gcc-lib/alpha-redhat-linux/egcs-2.91.66/

in other words, if you want to compile lala.c:

ccc -I/usr/lib/g... -o lala lala.c -L/usr/lib/g...

also there is a wrong link in 

usr/lib/compaq/ccc-6.2/alpha-redhat-linux/bin

ld is linked to some inexistent crap, instead remove the 
link and relink it to:

ld -> /usr/bin/ld

this, assuming that you have redhat6.0 and egcs-2.91.66.

cheers and good luck, h.

