Neither Linux or Windows (or Unix generally) have any 
solution to the library problem. That doesn't mean that 
perfectly good solutions don't exist. Explicit versioning, 
explicit installation instead of throw it in a directory 
and add it to the path, prevent libraries being overwritten 
if a registered application needs them - there is 
absolutely no reason why libraries should cause difficulty.

It is of course one of the rules in advocacy that one out 
of Windows, Linux/Unix or MacOS is perfect, and that the 
rest is crap. This means that major failings common to all 
three OS's are accepted by everyone.

