about
30 OEM PC164 based 500MHz Alpha PC's with 64MB ram (4x16MB 36bit),
4 GB western digital IDE drive, cdrom, S3 VirgeVX based PCI VGA and ISA
soundcard which were 'given away' for about $500. The IDE drive actually
*does*
kill performance but fortunately I had an ultra SCSI adapter and drive,
which I
could switch with the IDE components. A network card is not really a
relevant
cost factor these days.
I am running SuSE Linux 6.1 AXP and Windows NT 4.0 without any problems.

