  I've used a SB AudioPCI standard and a SB PCI128, both based on the
es1370 chip in my Alpha.  AFAIK, the es1371 is mostly the same as the
es1370.  Most of my testing has been done with RH6.0, Kernel 2.2.5. 
First thing, the free es1370 module is not fully OSS compatible.  It
won't show anything in /dev/sndstat, that is normal behavior.  Second,
the es1370 chip doesn't have a midi synth of anykind.  I'm not familiar
with mplay, is it a software midi synth? That's the only thing that will
work.  You do get two dsp's though, /dev/dsp and /dev/dsp1.
  The es1370 also was very noisy and poor quality on the Alpha.  Sine
waves got horribly corrupted, and I switched back to a cheap ISA card. 
Both of the cards sound great under Intel/Linux.  I guess there is
something different with the PCI bus.

Feldner & Braun GdbR wrote:
