Ricardo Ciria <ricardo@ibt.unam.mx> writes:

>   I am exporting filesystems from two RH Linux boxes (PC with 3.03 and 
>Alpha with 6.0) to a Spark with Solaris 2.7.
>
>   Everything betwen the Solaris and the PC works very well, but when I 
>access the files NFS-ed from the Alpha in the Solaris (a simple "ls", by 
>example), I get the Solaris message :
>
> "Value too large for defined data type". (there is a little example 
>   below), that means some kind of overflow.

It looks like you did a "ls -l".  That is far more complex than a simple
"ls" in that "-l" entails doing a stat(2) on every file maybe a readlink(2)
on some.

I suspect Solaris is complaining about inode numbers >= 2^31, i.e. with
the sign bit set.  I'd have to see some tcpdump data (and maybe
the raw hex) to be sure.  Try doing "ls -i" on client and server to get
better ideas.

	-Ric Werme
