For some weeks I have been running S@H on my Alpha under Linux using the
alpha-dec-osf3.0 vers 3.0 binary and some OSF 4.0 libraries.  It has been
working fine and giving me WU times around 7 hrs 40 mins.

A few days ago I tried running it from a RAM disc to see if I could get the
hard drive to spin down.  It was not entirely successful, so I reverted to
my previous configuration.

Imagine my horror when I discovered that my WU times had increased to about
9 hrs.  Things which I have done to try and fix the problem.

1) Stop and restart seti client.

2) Reboot machine ensuring that RAM disc module (rd.o) is not loaded.

3) Switch to previous OS version (2.2.11).

4) Copy client to new empty directory and start from scatch.

I am starting to run out of ideas :-(

System is 533 MHz 21164a (LX164) with 2 Mb cache running RedHat 6.0 with
2.2.12 kernel.

I use the Tru64 version of Netscape and that still works fine (although I
don't think that I would notice a 20% slowdown).[B

Does anyone have any ideas? 

