Well, let's see...last year about this time (or maybe a little later),
Lockheed Martin Corporation rolled out a corporate-wide email system called
LM Express. They bought a boatload of Alphaserver 4000s, and NT Server and
Exchange Server to run on them. The rollout was less than smooth, users were
thoroughly hacked off, the systems were unstable for the first little while,
and nobody at LM Enterprise Information Systems seemed to care much.

