Here are some detailed installation instructions for and AS200 (similar to
multia):

http://home.att.net/~sltackett/as200/as200.html

A good reference on milo and such is:

http://www.alphalinux.org/faq/milo-6.html

I use three disks.

#1: has linload.exe & milo <- this is a DOS diskette
#2: is an image of the generic.img from cdrom/images/
#3: is an image of the ramdisk.img from cdrom/images/

(used rawrite.com from dosutils to make the image)

I boot off of disk #1, get to Milo> prompt.

Put disk 2 in the drive and
issue the command:

boot fd0:vmlinux.gz root=/dev/fd0 load_ramdisk=1

Then it'll start booting and prompt you for a ramdisk floppy, then insert #3
and press enter and you should go right into the setup.

I have questions that I'm afraid to ask..

