Hello All

Does anyone have any information on 3d cards which have support under
Alpha\Linux?  It seems that Alpha\Linux is currently in pretty
sad shape in this respect.  One would think that both 3d modeling
and 3d games would be especially suited to 21164 and 21264 Alpha
systems with their superior floating point performace.  Why has this
never been exploited?

The 600 MHz LX machine that I currently have is generally used for Monte
Carlo simulations of nuclear/particle physics experiments and
data analysis, but it sure would be nice to play Quake2 Arena when
it is sitty idle.

-Eric Christy




