Jo Schambach wrote:


> Does someone have detailed instructions on how to boot a JENSEN to
> install Redhat Linux 6.0?

First you need a file called lxboot (which is the first sector of your hard
disk, I think) and a file called lxboot (which you can find
on the Redhat CD in the /boot directory)
Then you need a 2.2.x - Kernel compiled for Jensen (with 1742 support, etc. -
and ramdisk and romfs- Support)
-the generic.gz won't work !!!!

Follow the Instructions of the JENSEN-Howto on  writing that to your
harddisk.

Now you should be able to boot and execute the install program from
ramdisk.gz.

But don't  have any hope that your problems are solves then.
You'll get lots of ugly error messages ("alpha_fp_emul: unexpected function
code 0x0 at 0x120010cd0")
and some important programs won't run (like gawk or ghostscript)

Redhat seems to have sopped supporting AXP150 systems in RH60.
Use RH52 (or maybe Debian is better - I personally have not tried until now)

Benjamin




