After struggling for days to try and get stuff going on mounting my WINDOZE
shares on my Linux box, trying to figure out how to do it without smbmount,
I FINALLY discovered that smbmount is simply not in the samba rpm's.  I
thought this was an oversight.  It is NOT.  linux-2.2.5, according to Red Hat,
does not have smbfs (samba file system) support FOR THE ALPHA and so smbmount
was not configured in.

I run 2.2.12 and with smbfs, I had to go to www.samba.org and download the
sources.  You them configure with:

configure --with-smbmount
make
make install

This will put your NEW binaries in
/usr/local/samba/bin

and not over write the RH 6.0 stuff.  Included in this directory is smbmount
and it functions perfectly with the later kernels.

I enclose the reply Red Hat sent to me:

To: bugzilla-owner@redhat.com, notting@redhat.com, rwmcgwier@home.com
Subject: [Bug 4817] Changed - samba configuration for Dec Alpha


http://developer.redhat.com/bugzilla/show_bug.cgi?id=4817


--- shadow/4817 Tue Aug 31 21:42:18 1999
+++ shadow/4817.tmp.30922       Thu Sep  2 13:11:31 1999
@@ -3,12 +3,12 @@
 Version: 6.0
 Platform: alpha
 OS/Version:
-Status: NEW
-Resolution:
+Status: RESOLVED
+Resolution: LATER
 Severity: high
 Priority: normal
 Component: samba
-AssignedTo: Red Hat Team 2
+AssignedTo: notting@redhat.com
 ReportedBy: rwmcgwier@home.com
 URL:
 Cc: bugzilla-owner@redhat.com
@@ -23,3 +23,9 @@

 This apparently was done with the 386 code and not the
 alpha
+
+------- Additional Comments From notting@redhat.com  09/02/99 13:11 -------
+smbfs mounting is not shipped on alpha because support isn't
+compiled into the kernel.
+
+When one changes, the other will.




