A new try got me that far:

1) Ftp the Firmware version 1.7 from ftp.digital.com
2) get the ARC utilities from the same site
3) "down"graded my firmware witht the source from 1)
4) Changed to the ARC console and booted it
4) used the "minlabel.exe" (using "Run a program") program to partition
the only disk on this
system as follows:
        1: 8MB ext2
        2: 140MB swap
        3: whole disk (type "unused")
        4: rest of disk, ext2
        others: 0MB
5) copied the kernels/generic.gz kernel from RH CD to a floppy using
rawrite.exe
6) used the copyboot.exe program from the ARC utilities to copy the
floppy from step 5 to partition 1 on my harddisk (i.e. copy fd0 to sda)
7) got back to SRM prompt
8) "boot dka0 -fl i" to boot
9) now I get the "aboot" prompt asking me for a kernel file.
10) I answered:
"1/vmlinux.gz load_ramdisk=1 root=/dev/sda4"
11) Now I see a bunch of message seemingly indicating that the kernel is
booted, it starts a few services, and then it stops with the last
message reading:
"Starting kswapd v 1.5"

It never continues beyond this point.
Since I am new to this, I don't know what to expect next. Anybody have
any pointers?

Any help would be appreciated


